solution.p:
First we must find this lines slope using the slope formula:
\begin{aligned}
\amp\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\
\amp= \frac{{24-\left(-6\right)}}{{-20-\left(-2\right)}}\\
\amp= \frac{{30}}{{-18}}
\end{aligned}
So the slope is {-{\frac{5}{3}}}\text{.} Using the point {\left(-2,-6\right)} and point-slope form, an equation for the line is y={-{\frac{5}{3}}\mathopen{}\left(x+2\right)-6}\text{.}

